{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat task.md && cat output_contract.md && cat requirements.md && cat northstar_update_2026-04-30.md && cat vendor_quotes.csv'","aggregated_output":"# Vendor Quote Selection\n\nYou are helping choose a vendor for an upcoming field operations order.\n\nRead all files in this folder. Choose the best vendor that satisfies the requirements and budget. If files conflict, use source dates and the recency rule in `requirements.md`.\n\nCreate the deliverables listed in `output_contract.md` inside an `answer/` folder in this task folder. The goal is to leave behind useful work artifacts that another operations teammate could review.\n\nYour work must make the source-resolution step, vendor screening step, and final purchasing recommendation visible as separate checkpoints.\n# Deliverable Contract\n\nCreate an `answer/` folder in this task folder, then create these three files inside it. The format may be Markdown tables or concise labeled sections, but the paths, filenames, and required facts must be present.\n\n## `answer/source_resolution.md`\n\nRecord which source is current for each vendor where source dates matter.\n\nRequired facts:\n\n- The recency rule from `requirements.md`.\n- The stale Northstar row in `vendor_quotes.csv` dated 2026-04-24.\n- The newer Northstar update in `northstar_update_2026-04-30.md`.\n- The effective Northstar terms used for screening: unit price, available quantity, delivery date, screen size, battery rating, rugged case status, and warranty months.\n\n## `answer/vendor_screen.md`\n\nScreen every vendor against the hard requirements.\n\nRequired facts:\n\n- One row or entry for each vendor in `vendor_quotes.csv`.\n- For each vendor: effective source used, eligible `yes` or `no`, total cost if the vendor is otherwise eligible, and the blocking requirement when ineligible.\n- Budget status for any eligible vendor.\n\n## `answer/purchase_recommendation.md`\n\nWrite the final recommendation for the purchasing teammate.\n\nRequired facts:\n\n- Selected vendor.\n- Quantity.\n- Unit price.\n- Total cost calculation.\n- Budget result.\n- Delivery date.\n- Short rejected-vendor summary.\n\nRules:\n\n- Use local files only.\n- Do not put the required deliverables in the task root; put them under `answer/`.\n- Extra scratch files are allowed, but scoring is based on the three named deliverables under `answer/`.\n# Requirements\n\nRequest date: 2026-04-30\n\nOrder need: 12 rugged tablets for the field inspection team.\n\nBudget maximum: $2,200 total, including all selected units and required included accessories.\n\nNeed-by date: delivery no later than 2026-05-17.\n\nHard requirements:\n\n- Quantity must be 12 units.\n- Screen size must be at least 10.0 inches.\n- Battery rating must be at least 10 hours.\n- Rugged case must be included in the quoted price.\n- Warranty must be at least 12 months.\n\nSelection rule:\n\n- Reject vendors that miss any hard requirement.\n- Among vendors that meet all hard requirements and fit the budget, select the lowest total cost.\n- If a vendor appears in more than one dated source and values conflict, use the newest dated source for that vendor.\n- Use local files only.\n# Northstar Update\n\nSource date: 2026-04-30\n\nVendor: Northstar\n\nNorthstar revised its quote after the baseline CSV was exported.\n\nUpdated terms:\n\n- Unit price: $178\n- Available quantity: 12\n- Delivery date: 2026-05-16\n- Screen size: 10.1 inches\n- Battery rating: 11 hours\n- Rugged case: included\n- Warranty: 12 months\n\nUse this source instead of the older `vendor_quotes.csv` Northstar row where they conflict.\nvendor,quote_date,unit_price_usd,available_quantity,delivery_date,screen_inches,battery_hours,rugged_case_included,warranty_months,notes\nNorthstar,2026-04-24,185,12,2026-05-16,10.1,11,yes,12,\"Baseline quote. See any newer vendor-specific updates before deciding.\"\nAtlas,2026-04-27,168,12,2026-05-18,10.1,12,yes,12,\"Lowest baseline price but delivery date is after the need-by date.\"\nBrightPath,2026-04-26,171,12,2026-05-15,9.7,10,yes,12,\"Screen is below the minimum requirement.\"\nCobalt,2026-04-25,176,12,2026-05-16,10.1,9,yes,12,\"Battery rating is below the minimum requirement.\"\nDockside,2026-04-26,182,11,2026-05-14,10.1,13,yes,12,\"Only eleven units are available.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
